==================================================
2. CHAIN OF KNOWLEDGE STRUCTURE
==================================================

CoK OBJECT TYPES:

- CLAIM
- FACT
- RULE
- ASSUMPTION
- HYPOTHESIS
- DERIVATION
- EVIDENCE
- GOAL
- ACTION
- EXPERIMENT
- TEST_RESULT
- CONTRADICTION

CoK RELATIONSHIPS:

- REQUIRES
- IMPLIES
- SUPPORTS
- CONTRADICTS
- DEPENDS_ON
- PRODUCES
- TESTS
- ALTERNATIVE_TO

EXAMPLE:

Claim A --------+
                |
                +--> Rule R --> Conclusion C
                |
Claim B --------+

Conclusion C ---+
                |
                +--> Rule S --> Conclusion E
                |
Claim D --------+

Each derivation retains:
- Globally stable object identifier
- Premises
- Applied inference rule
- Assumptions and conditions
- Supporting evidence
- Source provenance
- Verification status
- Dependency references
- Schema version

KNOWLEDGE STATES:

PROVISIONAL
VERIFIED
DISPUTED
INVALIDATED
UNRESOLVED
ARCHIVED

Verified derivations may become reusable premises.

Invalidated derivations remain traceable.

Unresolved derivations may be revisited when new
evidence becomes available.

Formal proof validity and empirical truth are
tracked separately.


