==================================================
5. MEMORY AND HARDWARE ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

TARGET HARDWARE:

CPU:
- General-purpose x86-64 / ARM64
- No dedicated GPU required
- Optional GPU acceleration

RAM:
- Target system: 8 GB
- GammaThink target budget: <= 3 GB
- Configurable memory limits

STORAGE:
- SSD-first architecture
- Knowledge archives primarily disk-resident
- RAM contains only active working data

RAM COMPONENTS:

- Neural interpreter
- Active reasoning state
- Search frontier
- Bounded knowledge cache
- Database buffers
- Runtime overhead

SSD COMPONENTS:

- Kiwix archives
- GKS snapshots
- Reasoning journal
- Persistent indexes
- Historical derivations
- Experimental evidence

MEMORY POLICY:

- Fixed configurable memory budget
- Evict inactive cached objects
- Preserve persistent objects on SSD
- Bound search frontier size
- Avoid loading complete archives
- Track actual resident memory usage


