14. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
==================================================

- Neural interpretation and symbolic reasoning
  remain separate.

- CPU-only operation remains supported.

- Knowledge archives remain disk-backed,
  modular and hot-swappable.

- Knowledge growth does not require proportional
  growth in application RAM.

- Every reusable derivation retains its
  assumptions and dependencies.

- Verification preserves evidence and provenance.

- Contradictions are not silently overwritten.

- Missing evidence is not equivalent to
  evidence of falsity.

- Failed search is not proof of impossibility.

- Offline reasoning remains possible with
  available local dependencies.

- Distributed contributions require permission.

- The reasoning graph can grow independently
  of the neural model's weights.


